---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<SiteLayout current="overview">
  <section class="landing-hero">
    <h1>Opinionated notes on building agents that actually ship.</h1>
    <p class="landing-lede">
      A set of opinionated notes for an internal sharing on agent
      engineering: what agents are, how they use tools, how to test them,
      and where Google ADK and CodeAct fit.
    </p>
    <div class="landing-anchors">
      <a href={url('/what-is-agent/')}>Start with the agent loop <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={url('/harness-engineering/')}>Skip to the harness <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-section landing-section--last">
    <div class="section-head compact-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Read in order</p>
      <h2>Full table of contents.</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="toc-list">
      <li><a href={url('/what-is-agent/')}><span>01</span><strong>What is an agent?</strong><em>Models in a control loop: state, tools, observations, and stopping criteria.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/session-state-memory/')}><span>01A</span><strong>Session, state, memory</strong><em>The current thread, the live scratchpad, and long-term searchable context.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/orchestration/')}><span>02</span><strong>Design patterns</strong><em>ReAct, planner-executor, reflection, multi-agent, graph, CodeAct — the six shapes an agent runs in.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/engineering-practice/')}><span>03</span><strong>Tools &amp; capability</strong><em>Function tools, MCP, skills, code execution, retrieval, and human handoff.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/function-tools/')}><span>03A</span><strong>Function tools</strong><em>The narrowest useful tool form.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/skills/')}><span>03B</span><strong>Skills</strong><em>Packaged repeatable know-how.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/code-execution/')}><span>03C</span><strong>Code execution</strong><em>Code execution as a tool form — the runtime piece behind CodeAct.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/eval-observability/')}><span>04</span><strong>Eval &amp; observability</strong><em>Traces explain what happened. Evals tell whether it was good enough.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/harness-engineering/')}><span>05</span><strong>Harness concept</strong><em>The runtime boundary around state, tools, permissions, replay, and tests.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/harness-examples/')}><span>05A</span><strong>ADK harness examples</strong><em>Runner, confirmations, HITL, evals, events — the harness made concrete.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/codeact/')}><span>06</span><strong>CodeAct Deep Dive</strong><em>The action shape that scales. Defended properly, with the trade-off named.</em></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/codeact-ds-agent/')}><span>06A</span><strong>A specialized ML agent</strong><em>End-to-end Kaggle workflow: function tool for the CLI, skill for the modeling sweep, CodeAct in between.</em></a></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
